      "message": "It depends on a newer version of AEMU, I think.  For Linux-distro style package management, it\u0027s desirable for older versions of AEMU to still.  That means a newer gfxstream can work with an older AEMU.  \n\nSome details regarding AEMU versioning still have to be worked out (https://buganizer.corp.google.com/issues/300166662).\n\nAs for removing setLogger, I think it\u0027s mostly useful for AEMU.  QEMU/crosvm/others has it\u0027s own logging infrastructure.  So the idea is to keep API churn to the bare minimum necessary.",
